/* ── The dashboard parts: action tiles, status rows, the facet list, the heat grid, the matrix, the bar in a cell, the
   week agenda and the run timeline [kpadopt2] ──
   Synthwave's own (themes/synthwave/CHARACTER.md): a tile is the tape, square, with the pink to cyan stripe along its
   top and the corners falling in the stripe's colours, never glowing on its rim (G6, G7); pointing turns the tube up in
   one step, the stripe and the title's tube (G8); a press charges it, the top edge burning near-white, and nothing
   moves (the register's press); a failure is the VCR's stop before the title, in the red (the register's tone); waiting
   is the marquee, bulbs
   chasing one in four, start to end, four hard steps a 900 ms loop (G10); what runs is the road, the lane dashes
   racing (G11, G16); the OSD's mono capitals name, the chrome counts (G15). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: what the package leaves to a register [kpadopt2-repairs] ──
   Formal keeps these parts exactly as Kenny approved them; this theme takes the three repairs the review asks for: a
   loading heat grid or matrix row as tall as its ready row (no skeleton gap between cells), an empty or failed run
   timeline with a lane-sized space for its sentence (never over the legend), the sentence as wide as its words on the
   theme's ground (never through a rule or a ghost bar), and an axis label near the end edge standing before its rule. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The six opt-in options of the dashboard adoption, round 3, in this theme [kpadopt3] ──
   The nav bar's separator, the timeline's day buttons and series runs, the week agenda's upcoming list on a phone and
   the facet swatch's identity pattern (the choice-filter value and the heat grid's End are behaviour only).
   Synthwave's own (themes/synthwave/CHARACTER.md): the separator is the horizon stood upright, the pink
   tube with its white core glowing; lying down across the phone's list it is the horizon itself. A day on the axis is
   swept by the laser under the pointer; pressed it is lit in the pink tube with its glow, the date in the core's white.
   A series' finished run glows in its own neon; the upcoming list's day rule is a line of the grid floor; the facet
   pattern glows in its hue. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in synthwave's own grammar [kpadopt4] ──
   Synthwave is the drive into the sunset (themes/synthwave/CHARACTER.md): the tape stands on the grid floor under its
   own horizon, every light is a neon tube, what arrives rises over its horizon and what leaves sets behind it (G2, G3,
   G12). A part that is drawn rises 0.5 rem from behind its line, uncovered from that line up, on the sunrise curve in
   two beats of 225 ms (G1, G4); light switches in hard steps and is never tweened (G1); pointing turns the tube up in one
   step (G8); a press dips it (G14); a warning is a hollow neon ring before the title or figure, the words glowing in the
   tone's ink (G13); a change draws the laser (G9); labels are the OSD's capitals after a cyan arrow, figures the chrome
   display (G15); square plates carrying the pink to cyan stripe, 2 px controls, never a notch or a pill (G6). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── end the kpadopt4 data pieces ── */

